  "reason": "The current best (config_019, scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + weighted, acc=0.706) represents a major jump from all scgpt-based configs. However, the avgpool-over-transformer advantage was only established with scgpt (config_010: 0.471 vs config_005: 0.512). scvi_n200 produces fundamentally different latent representations, and transformer attention could capture cross-profile interactions that simple averaging misses. config_031 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) is the only untested combination that directly tests this uncertainty with the best-performing encoders. It is the highest-information experiment that could either break through the 0.706 ceiling or confirm avgpool is optimal, guiding the remaining 4 experiments. Expected relative cost: moderate-to-high (~7-9 GPU hours), roughly 1.5-2× the avgpool variants, due to the transformer aggregation layer over multiple profiles. This is justified because it is the single most likely path to a new best accuracy, and 4 experiments remain to exploit any gain."
}

